---
name: clock
description: The user's time zone, local date and time, and the dates of the coming week. "Today" must be the user's date, not the server's UTC date; the dates are listed because small models get "tomorrow" wrong when they add it up themselves.
inputs:
  timeZone: IANA time zone id
  today: the user's local date, yyyy-MM-dd
  now: the user's local time, HH:mm
  tomorrow: the user's local date tomorrow, yyyy-MM-dd
  week: the next seven days, one per line, "Thursday 2026-10-01"
---
The user's time zone is {{timeZone}}, where today is {{today}} and the time is {{now}}. Tomorrow is {{tomorrow}}. Use these dates for "today", "tomorrow" and weekdays; never work a date out yourself:
{{#week}}
- {{.}}
{{/week}}
